        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Sample of Jacquard woven silk dress fabric, probably made in Great Britain, ca. 1840-1850."@en , "Sample of figured silk dress fabric. The pattern shows broad, bright blue satin stripes bordered with cream, alternating  with areas of black satin ground woven with a Japanese design. The design is Jacquard woven in red, blue and white on a black satin ground and shows large fan shapes filled with stylised flowers superimposed on a delicate floral trail. There is a selvedge at one side."@en ;
